  "title": "Kirby Problem 3.65",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $S_{2,\\infty}(Y)$ denote the Kauffman bracket skein module of a closed, oriented 3-manifold $Y$; this is a module over $R=\\mathbb{Z}[A,A^{-1}]$. For $Y$ prime and connected, does $S_{2,\\infty}(Y)$ having rank one, in the sense that\n\n$$\nS_{2,\\infty}(Y)\\otimes_R \\mathbb{Q}(A)\\cong \\mathbb{Q}(A),\n$$\n\nimply that $Y$ is $S^3$ or $S^1\\times S^2$?",
